/*
    Core revenue measures — the single source of truth (requirement #1).
    Live in a dedicated, column-less "_Measures" table.
    Every one has a Description (shown here as a comment) and a Display Folder
    set in the model metadata (noted below) so report authors find them without
    guessing.

    Display Folder: "Revenue"
*/

Gross Sales :=
SUMX ( 'Fact Sales', 'Fact Sales'[GrossAmountLocal] )
-- Description: Gross order value before returns or rebates, in transaction
-- local currency. Not comparable across currencies without a conversion measure.

Returns :=
SUMX ( 'Fact Sales', 'Fact Sales'[ReturnsAmountLocal] )
-- Description: Value of returned goods, local currency, negative convention
-- (stored as positive in the fact table, subtracted here).

Rebates :=
SUMX ( 'Fact Sales', 'Fact Sales'[RebatesAmountLocal] )
-- Description: Distributor rebates/discounts accrued against the order, local currency.

Net Revenue :=
[Gross Sales] - [Returns] - [Rebates]
-- Description: THE revenue number. Gross Sales less Returns less Rebates.
-- This is the only measure any report should use for "revenue" — there is no
-- second definition anywhere else in the model.

Cost :=
SUMX ( 'Fact Sales', 'Fact Sales'[CostLocal] )
-- Description: Cost of goods sold, local currency. Subject to Object-Level
-- Security — see security/ols_notes.md. Hidden from roles below Director.

Margin :=
[Net Revenue] - [Cost]
-- Description: Net Revenue less Cost. Also OLS-protected.

Margin % :=
DIVIDE ( [Margin], [Net Revenue] )
-- Description: Margin as a percentage of Net Revenue. OLS-protected (depends on Margin).
